    "title": "Lumberjack Community Raises Over $137,000 on Giving Tuesday to Support Local Student Needs - NewsBreak",
    "text": "3 hours ago On Giving Tuesday, the Lumberjack community raised $137,940 from 264 donors. This amount is $8,592 more than last year. The funds will support student needs such as environmental research, emergency assistance, and Louie’s Cupboard. Louie’s Cupboard received $11,525, which triggered an additional $50,000 gift from Terence and Robin Roche. This funding will provide 4,101 Grab & Go grocery bags.\nGiving Tuesday Champions raised $21,915 through peer-to-peer outreach. An anonymous donor’s $12,000 challenge funded 37 LEAF grants. The effort included 180 alumni, 112 faculty and staff, and 28 parents and family members. Alumni from the 1990s contributed the most. Thirty-one people made their first gift to NAU.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
